From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Seer: source settings saved in the database, applied without a restart

The .env source settings can be overridden from the UI. Overrides live in the property
table; secrets (Soulseek, Lidarr and Spotify keys) are sealed with AES-256-GCM using
seer.key, a 0600 file next to the database. Saving rebuilds the sources and the playlist
reader at once; running requests keep the sources they started with.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
